  "hypothesis": "Potential-Field Gradient-Tensor Source Dimensionality (quasi-2D step-source shape index) with cross-field strike agreement, scale persistence and incumbent-proximity novelty allocation",
  "mechanism": "For GeoDAWN B02 rtp, B13 iso_grav_anom and B15 depth_to_base_surf, Gaussian-derivative structure tensors J = G*grad(F)grad(F)^T and Hessians at sigma = 2 and 5 px. Closed-form 2x2 eigenvalues give linearity L = (lam1-lam2)/(lam1+lam2) (~1 for an elongated quasi-2D step source such as a buried faulted basement contact, ~0 for equant 3-D bodies), energetic step score S = L * E, cross-field axial strike agreement cos(2*dtheta), sigma5/sigma2 scale persistence (deep fault steps persist; shallow volcanic texture decays), an explicit equant-source mimic channel (1-L)*E, and a cover-gated joint score (strong subsurface step, weak surface slope B19). GTD-14 channels are strictly zero-catalogue (existing_faults.tif / grid.catalogue never read in feature construction) and are appended to the cached PHYS-44 + HGVC-20 + BPWD PSGV-20 stacks inside the identical dual-expectation LightGBM specialists, distance-adaptive tri-specialist Log-Odds PoE and exact Dinkelbach allocator as H88-BPWD, so the paired same-fold contrast isolates the GTD marginal contribution. Production additionally applies a preregistered incumbent-proximity discount w = 0.55 + 0.45*clip(d/3px,0,1) versus shipped BPWD+HGVC+H33 dots (fold-fair analogue in holdout: versus that fold's BPWD-control dots) to keep the emission in its own lane instead of reselecting incumbent crests (the IR-88-127 / IR-88-249E-02 failure mode).",
